    "body": "i think Nushell handles *empty values* out-of-the-box.\r\nthere is the `null` value which is passed if an argument is not defined, e.g. with the following mockup of the init script,\r\n```bash\r\ndef starship [-a: any, -b: any, -c: any] {\r\n    print $\"a: ($a)\"\r\n    print $\"b: ($b)\"\r\n    print $\"c: ($c)\"\r\n}\r\n\r\ndef init [-a: any, -b: any, -c: any] {\r\n    starship -a $a -b $b -c $c\r\n}\r\n```\r\n`init ...` with any combination of options works just fine :relieved: \r\n\r\nalso i think `$env.CMD_DURATION_MS`, `$env.LAST_EXIT_CODE` and `term size` will always return something :+1: \r\n\r\ni think this is safe and more clean, you tell me of course :yum: ",
